description:
Must be able to obtain Baseline 
12 + 12 month contract
6+ years working with SQL, SAS, R, and/or Python
Our client an independent statutory agency which supports a better life for hundreds of thousands of Australians with a significant and permanent disability and their families and carers, is looking for the services of a Senior Data Analyst.
Key Duties and Responsibilities
Active participation in small, multi-disciplinary teams, in the design, build, deployment and maintenance of data assets and data products in the NDIAs cloud data platform;
Presentation of complex technical options, decisions and results tailored to audiences with different levels of technical and data literacy;
Data wrangling, profiling and quality assessment of new or changed data sources and new data integrations;
Design and prototype development of new data attributes and products;
Data validation testing including defect and anomaly remediation.
Skills and Experience Required 
Extensive data analysis experience with a strong ability to prototype high-quality solutions from complex disparate datasets;
Proven ability to work independently with a clear purpose and deliver high-quality outcomes with limited supervision under tight deadlines;
Ability to work as part of a team with active collaboration, sharing of skills and capacity;
Experience working within an industrialised Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW) environment and understanding of data pipelines, modelling and data and reporting platform architectures.

How to Apply
For a copy of the full job description, including the application instructions, please get in touch with Daniel at Recruitment Hive by clicking the Quick Apply button.  Alternatively you can reach Daniel on (02) 6299 1*** to discuss further.
Please note that applications close on Thursday the 30th July 2026 at midday. Recruitment Hive welcome late applications to be considered for future opportunities.
Job ID: DE673663 | LH-07240 
We Value Diversity
The Recruitment Hive is a proud Equal Opportunity Employer. We recognise the value of diverse perspectives and experience and are committed to an inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and respected for who they are. We encourage people with disability, indigenous, veterans and people of all backgrounds and abilities to express their interest in this role.
